DismantleMode [SimTalk]
Sets how the DismantleStation designated by <Path> handles the MUs.
Remarks
The Dismantle Mode provides these settings:
• Detach MUs: The DismantleStation detaches the mounting parts from the main MU and moves them
on to the successor which you typed into the Dismantle Table. If you only want to unload those
mounting parts from the main MU, which type into the Dismantle Table, select Sequence > MUs
exiting independent of other MUs or Main MU after other MUs and the Dismantle Mode > Detach
MUs. Always type a valid MU class into the column MU and a positive number into the column Number.
• Create MUs: The DismantleStation creates mounting parts.
Type
Read-only attribute
DismantleMode [SimTalk]
11-1858 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Syntax
<Path>.DismantleMode:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
Specify "Create MUs" to create MUs.
Specify "Detach MUs" to detach them from the main MU.
Example
MyDismantleStation.DismantleMode := "Detach MUs"
See also
Dismantle Table [button] - DismantleStation
Sequence [drop-down list] - DismantleStation
Dismantle Mode [drop-down list] - DismantleStation
