ExitingMUMode [SimTalk]
Sets if the main MU exits the DismantleStation designated by <Path> or if a new MU will be created which
then exits the object.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ExitingMUMode:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify "Main MU" or "New MU".
• Main MU: The DismantleStation moves the main MU on to the succeeding object.
• New MU: The DismantleStation deletes the main MU, creates a new MU, and moves it on to the
successor. The DismantleStation then shows the text box MU.
Type the path to the class of the new MU into the text box, or click the button 
  and select the new MU
in the dialog Select Object.
Example
MyDismantleStation.ExitingMUMode := "New MU"
See also
Exiting MU [drop-down list] - DismantleStation
ExitingMUMode [SimTalk]
